WEBVTT

00:12.978 --> 00:14.021
I'm home.

00:14.938 --> 00:15.939
Yota!

00:16.606 --> 00:18.942
- I'm so sorry about earlier.
- Huh?

00:19.651 --> 00:22.446
<i>You must feel annoyed for a family member
to come and talk to you</i>

00:22.529 --> 00:24.072
<i>when you're with a friend.</i>

00:24.614 --> 00:25.615
MUMBLE MUMBLE

00:25.699 --> 00:28.076
Oh, goodness. And you are at that age...

00:28.160 --> 00:30.912
- No. It's fine.
- Why did I call out to you?

00:34.750 --> 00:36.501
Thanks for the food.

00:38.045 --> 00:39.129
Come on, now.

00:40.088 --> 00:42.424
No fair! Haruto's getting all the fun.

00:42.507 --> 00:44.426
Could you wait until I'm done eating?

00:44.509 --> 00:47.053
- Now!
- So loud!

00:48.764 --> 00:50.724
You two...

00:50.807 --> 00:51.808
RUMBLE RUMBLE

00:51.892 --> 00:52.893
WHOOSH

00:52.976 --> 00:55.312
- Stop bothering your brother!
- Daddy!

00:57.898 --> 01:00.650
- Do the airplane again!
- Do it!

01:00.734 --> 01:02.819
- Daddy's done for now.
- Come on!

01:02.903 --> 01:04.404
Wanna tag out?

01:04.488 --> 01:07.074
You don't have to do anything, Yota.

01:07.157 --> 01:08.158
You kids.

01:08.241 --> 01:09.242
Thanks.

01:14.873 --> 01:16.041
Daddy!

01:16.124 --> 01:17.834
NOISY NOISY

01:24.800 --> 01:29.721
<i>The sounds of the day
swirl around and around in my head.</i>

01:36.353 --> 01:38.188
<i>I have to stop the noise,</i>

01:39.397 --> 01:40.899
<i>or it consumes me.</i>

01:42.776 --> 01:43.860
<i>Nothing.</i>

01:45.654 --> 01:47.489
<i>Think of nothing.</i>

01:51.952 --> 01:55.038
<i>I have one little sister,
and one little brother.</i>

01:55.122 --> 01:57.457
<i>And I tell you what, man,
are they stubborn!</i>

01:57.999 --> 02:00.836
<i>We were trying to decide
what to have for dinner the other day,</i>

02:00.919 --> 02:04.631
<i>and my sister said, "I want pasta!"
but my brother said, "I want curry!"</i>

02:04.714 --> 02:07.134
<i>Neither would budge. And then...</i>

02:07.217 --> 02:09.845
My younger brother and sister
are still little.

02:09.928 --> 02:11.638
It's too noisy at home.

02:12.472 --> 02:14.891
- Have you been out here all this time?
- Yeah.

02:17.894 --> 02:20.772
But I want to spend some time zoning out.

02:21.940 --> 02:24.526
<i>The more I think about it,</i>

02:25.735 --> 02:28.697
<i>the more the words he's said
start falling into place.</i>

02:30.657 --> 02:32.659
<i>But even if I am right about this,</i>

02:33.952 --> 02:36.496
<i>is this really something
I should be getting involved in?</i>

02:37.956 --> 02:41.001
<i>If someone says they're fine,</i>

02:41.585 --> 02:43.170
<i>who am I to worry?</i>

02:44.754 --> 02:47.174
<i>Who am I to intrude further?</i>

04:19.557 --> 04:23.937
EPISODE 7
LONELINESS AND SOLITUDE

04:24.020 --> 04:25.313
YUISHIRO

04:25.397 --> 04:26.856
Listen, Koyuki.

04:27.482 --> 04:30.360
Your father and I are getting a divorce.

04:32.195 --> 04:33.196
LOVEBIRDS

04:33.280 --> 04:37.367
<i>I knew they weren't like those
perfect couples you see on TV.</i>

04:37.450 --> 04:38.743
I don't think that.

04:38.827 --> 04:43.123
- <i>I knew they argued when I wasn't looking.</i>
- I work myself to the bone, you know?

04:43.707 --> 04:47.335
<i>I knew. I knew all this.</i>

04:49.087 --> 04:50.839
<i>And yet...</i>

04:51.923 --> 04:54.092
<i>I still felt safe in the knowledge</i>

04:54.884 --> 04:58.138
<i>that Mom and I were close,
and that Dad loved me.</i>

04:59.097 --> 05:02.434
<i>I felt confident that those things
would keep them together.</i>

05:04.060 --> 05:06.604
<i>I thought it would all work out.</i>

05:07.605 --> 05:09.649
<i>But was I in fact someone...</i>

05:11.276 --> 05:12.277
YUISHIRO - HIKAWA

05:13.111 --> 05:15.238
<i>...that Dad could live without?</i>

05:20.327 --> 05:22.871
Her water bottle is so lame.
Like, it literally makes me laugh.

05:22.954 --> 05:24.748
Stop it, Manatsu.

05:26.374 --> 05:28.376
<i>I didn't fit in.</i>

05:28.460 --> 05:32.297
<i>I never felt like I belonged,
no matter where I went.</i>

05:33.465 --> 05:37.594
Koyun, what do you find
so repulsive about Igarashi?

05:37.677 --> 05:38.803
I feel sorry for the guy.

05:40.472 --> 05:43.808
<i>I felt empty, not being able
to share my feelings with anyone.</i>

05:44.976 --> 05:46.311
<i>I thought what if...</i>

05:47.103 --> 05:52.776
<i>What if nobody really cares
whether I'm around or not?</i>

05:54.027 --> 05:57.030
<i>The thoughts crept in,</i>

05:57.614 --> 05:59.449
<i>and slowly tore at my heart.</i>

06:01.409 --> 06:03.828
CLUB WITHDRAWAL FORM

06:09.459 --> 06:10.919
<i>Back then,</i>

06:12.212 --> 06:14.631
<i>being with others
was when I felt most alone.</i>

06:19.928 --> 06:22.347
GRADE 1 CLASS 2

06:22.430 --> 06:23.431
WHEW... WHEW...

06:23.515 --> 06:24.599
<i>Yota is not me.</i>

06:25.308 --> 06:27.602
<i>His circumstances
are completely different to mine.</i>

06:27.685 --> 06:29.604
YOTA - WHAT TIME DO YOU FINISH
CLUB ACTIVITIES TODAY?

06:30.313 --> 06:34.609
<i>What's right to me
and what's right to him may be different.</i>

06:35.944 --> 06:38.696
<i>But still, I feel like I understand.</i>

06:39.197 --> 06:40.198
Go!

06:41.407 --> 06:45.120
<i>I know how lonely it feels
to be around others</i>

06:45.203 --> 06:47.205
<i>and still feel like you don't belong.</i>

06:50.667 --> 06:51.876
<i>Koyun?</i>

06:52.669 --> 06:57.507
<i>Probably around dismiss--</i>

07:01.094 --> 07:02.720
Hey, your phone!

07:04.722 --> 07:05.765
Geez.

07:06.474 --> 07:07.559
KOYUKI

07:07.642 --> 07:08.977
<i>Koyun?</i>

07:09.060 --> 07:12.021
Sorry about that. Thank you.

07:13.231 --> 07:14.524
<i>I saw it.</i>

07:16.609 --> 07:18.528
PROBABLY AN UPRISING

07:19.112 --> 07:20.989
<i>What does that mean?</i>

07:22.866 --> 07:23.867
PROBABLY AROUND DISMISSAL

07:23.950 --> 07:25.285
SORRY, TYPO! LOL

07:26.661 --> 07:28.288
PFFT

07:28.371 --> 07:30.540
BLAZING CHINESE GYOSHO

07:31.499 --> 07:36.254
And then I dropped my phone
before I could fix it, and it sent.

07:37.505 --> 07:40.049
I was like, "What kind of typo was that?"

07:40.133 --> 07:41.134
BIG HANDS

07:41.217 --> 07:43.553
I'm not very good at typing on my phone.

07:44.137 --> 07:45.138
Grandpa.

07:45.221 --> 07:47.640
I have superseded "Dad" now.

07:50.643 --> 07:52.729
Sorry for dragging you out like this.

07:52.812 --> 07:54.063
I don't mind.

07:59.527 --> 08:00.778
So...

08:01.362 --> 08:02.572
My...

08:03.323 --> 08:04.824
My parents are divorced.

08:04.908 --> 08:05.909
Huh?

08:09.746 --> 08:12.123
Which means I'm on my own a lot
when I get home.

08:13.249 --> 08:16.211
So if you're free,
and it doesn't have to be all the time,

08:18.171 --> 08:21.799
but I'd really like it
if you'd help me kill time after school.

08:26.304 --> 08:27.472
I'd like that.

08:31.392 --> 08:33.478
That's very kind of you, Koyun.

08:33.561 --> 08:35.313
Huh? No, it's not.

08:35.396 --> 08:37.732
I'm so narrow-minded,
and I'm quick to anger.

08:37.815 --> 08:39.234
That's not true.

08:42.320 --> 08:45.240
I see you as a kind person.

08:49.244 --> 08:50.245
Sorry, but...

08:51.496 --> 08:54.499
can we have a chat for a little?

08:55.667 --> 08:56.668
Sure.

09:03.633 --> 09:08.137
Ever since Mom passed away,
Dad has always been super busy.

09:08.763 --> 09:11.516
He never makes it
to any school events either.

09:12.350 --> 09:14.769
PARENT VISITATION DAY

09:15.478 --> 09:19.190
<i>I tried not to think about it
during parent visitation days.</i>

09:19.274 --> 09:20.275
FIDGETY
LOOKY LOOKY

09:24.821 --> 09:25.905
<i>And then...</i>

09:25.989 --> 09:28.658
Hello, Yota. It's nice to meet you.

09:29.367 --> 09:30.910
You're very tall.

09:30.994 --> 09:32.287
This is Akari.

09:33.037 --> 09:36.541
<i>Dad introduced me to my current mom.</i>

09:37.917 --> 09:40.128
Sorry, he's very shy around others.

09:40.211 --> 09:42.130
Yota. No need to force it, okay?

09:42.213 --> 09:43.798
UM... UM...

09:44.924 --> 09:48.136
<i>Mom is very nice to me.</i>

09:55.393 --> 09:56.394
<i>But...</i>

09:58.146 --> 10:00.565
Akari! I think I can get
my paternity leave.

10:01.149 --> 10:02.817
- Really?
- Yeah.

10:02.900 --> 10:05.528
- I'm so happy! Thank you.
- Finally.

10:06.237 --> 10:08.323
<i>Sometimes I wonder.</i>

10:09.365 --> 10:11.534
I told you so.

10:11.618 --> 10:13.661
<i>Do I even exist?</i>

10:15.288 --> 10:21.628
<i>I feel like I'm the only one
who is different in my family.</i>

10:24.380 --> 10:26.090
I know I'm probably
just being overdramatic,

10:27.383 --> 10:29.802
but once I start,
I can't stop thinking about it...

10:31.721 --> 10:33.306
I'm always running away from it.

10:39.270 --> 10:43.566
Yota. You can't blame yourself
for your thoughts or the way you feel.

10:44.067 --> 10:46.319
<i>I get it so much that it hurts.</i>

10:47.445 --> 10:51.324
You may be wrestling with
"why do I think like this?"

10:52.784 --> 10:55.244
But the more you blame yourself,

10:55.912 --> 10:59.248
you start to despise yourself, right?

10:59.749 --> 11:03.628
<i>You can run away from your environment,
but you can't run away from yourself.</i>

11:06.214 --> 11:08.132
You're amazing, Koyun.

11:10.134 --> 11:11.344
You see right through me.

11:22.355 --> 11:24.774
Hey, Koyun? You're crying?

11:24.857 --> 11:27.276
Don't mind me.

11:27.360 --> 11:30.947
This is just like a glitch in my system
when I can't process my emotions.

11:31.030 --> 11:33.157
- What?
- I get it all the time.

11:33.241 --> 11:34.450
Huh?

11:35.785 --> 11:38.371
<i>He is different in gender,
in build, and in personality.</i>

11:38.955 --> 11:42.250
<i>He is so different to me,
and I envied him for that.</i>

11:43.876 --> 11:49.257
<i>I thought Yota's kindness came
from his strength of heart and composure.</i>

11:50.716 --> 11:53.678
<i>But if it's because he bottles things in,
or if he's given up already...</i>

11:54.887 --> 11:57.390
<i>That would be heartbreaking for him.</i>

11:59.851 --> 12:03.146
Yota. You don't have to be
a "good" person.

12:05.356 --> 12:08.025
So please don't torture yourself.

12:13.614 --> 12:16.534
SIGH

12:17.410 --> 12:21.205
Thank you, Koyun.
Sorry for talking about such weird things.

12:21.747 --> 12:23.916
No, it's not weird at all.

12:25.293 --> 12:28.129
I've never talked about this
with anyone before.

12:29.130 --> 12:32.008
Definitely never talked about it
with Minato, or anyone like that.

12:32.091 --> 12:36.179
You really love Amamiya, don't you?

12:37.388 --> 12:38.389
Not really?

12:38.973 --> 12:40.308
If you say so.

12:41.434 --> 12:44.687
And if I can be of any help,
I'm all ears if you need me.

12:45.897 --> 12:48.941
When you bottle things in, your heart...
It, like...

12:49.484 --> 12:52.153
It eventually just gets covered in soot.

12:52.653 --> 12:53.696
Soot?

12:53.779 --> 12:55.198
Yes. Soot.

12:55.281 --> 12:58.117
When it builds up,
it clouds your outlook on life.

12:58.201 --> 13:00.703
- Before you know it, you're stuck.
- <i>Soot, soot!</i>

13:01.204 --> 13:03.039
<i>Soot, soot...</i>

13:04.665 --> 13:05.917
I see.

13:06.000 --> 13:07.251
That does make sense.

13:19.555 --> 13:20.932
What do I do?

13:23.518 --> 13:25.978
Koyun. I gotta tell you.

13:35.613 --> 13:36.864
I...

13:38.824 --> 13:41.619
I'm in love.

13:43.788 --> 13:44.789
What?

13:53.923 --> 13:56.759
I'm in love.

13:58.886 --> 13:59.887
What?

14:02.557 --> 14:04.767
With Miki...

14:12.483 --> 14:14.402
What? What?

14:14.485 --> 14:18.322
You mean "love" love? Not like? "Love"?

14:18.406 --> 14:19.407
PANIC - EEK

14:24.245 --> 14:25.413
Both.

14:27.498 --> 14:28.916
No way.

14:29.000 --> 14:31.002
I had no idea!

14:31.085 --> 14:33.087
But you're always so calm?

14:33.588 --> 14:36.048
No, I'm really not.

14:36.549 --> 14:37.550
PANICKING INSIDE

14:37.633 --> 14:40.428
I'm always a total mess
whenever I'm around Miki.

14:41.012 --> 14:43.431
What? No, you're no--

14:49.103 --> 14:50.104
<i>You are.</i>

14:50.605 --> 14:52.231
MIDDLE SCHOOL
DO YOU LIKE MIKI?

14:52.315 --> 14:54.191
Minato's known for a while now.

14:54.275 --> 14:55.860
- NO, WHY WOULD YOU SAY THAT?
- YEAH, RIGHT...

14:55.943 --> 14:57.486
But he bugs me, so I just deny it.

14:57.570 --> 14:59.530
<i>I guess you would feel embarrassed.</i>

15:00.448 --> 15:04.452
<i>Wow, now what? This makes me so happy!</i>

15:05.912 --> 15:08.247
What's the real me?

15:08.748 --> 15:10.875
I don't know what I'm feeling anymore.

15:10.958 --> 15:15.296
Don't go creating an ideal version of me
and then get disappointed!

15:15.379 --> 15:16.380
GRRR!

15:16.464 --> 15:20.843
<i>Miki. Somebody likes you for you.
Just the way you are.</i>

15:21.969 --> 15:25.139
<i>And he's such a wonderful person.</i>

15:28.225 --> 15:29.226
FIDGET FIDGET

15:29.310 --> 15:31.562
Are you going to ask her out?

15:31.646 --> 15:34.482
Koyun? Where did all
this energy come from?

15:34.565 --> 15:36.067
Sorry. I'm just happy.

15:36.150 --> 15:37.151
(SUPER HAPPY DANCE)

15:37.902 --> 15:38.903
<i>But...</i>

15:43.282 --> 15:44.867
<i>How does Miki feel?</i>

15:46.994 --> 15:48.871
I haven't thought that far ahead.

15:50.456 --> 15:53.250
Or rather,
I don't even plan on telling her.

15:54.543 --> 15:57.755
I just like her. I like Miki.

15:59.048 --> 16:01.801
And I value her as a friend as well.

16:03.219 --> 16:07.848
I know she probably
doesn't see me in the same way.

16:09.308 --> 16:10.393
But...

16:11.227 --> 16:15.064
<i>I feel like as time goes on,
it feels like I'm just deceiving her.</i>

16:16.232 --> 16:19.652
I'm starting to feel like I need
to apologize for liking her.

16:19.735 --> 16:20.861
WHOA!

16:20.945 --> 16:23.239
Didn't I tell you not to torture yourself?

16:23.322 --> 16:24.532
<i>Soot, soot...</i>

16:27.618 --> 16:29.870
Don't tell anybody
what we talked about today.

16:29.954 --> 16:31.038
Of course I won't.

16:31.622 --> 16:35.501
I'm absolutely rooting for you,
but I won't do anything to give you away.

16:36.919 --> 16:37.920
Thanks.

16:41.507 --> 16:42.842
Feels like a thumb.

16:42.925 --> 16:43.968
It is my pinky.

16:45.511 --> 16:49.473
I'm glad we became friends, Koyun.

16:53.519 --> 16:54.520
Me too.

16:57.481 --> 16:59.316
Yota, welcome home.

16:59.400 --> 17:00.568
I'm home.

17:01.402 --> 17:03.070
STARE

17:03.612 --> 17:05.197
Did you take a detour home?

17:05.281 --> 17:06.282
EEP

17:06.365 --> 17:08.200
<i>Did I get home too late?</i>

17:08.284 --> 17:10.953
Yeah, I was with a friend.

17:11.037 --> 17:12.204
I knew it.

17:12.288 --> 17:16.959
You look happy, so I thought
something good must have happened.

17:17.043 --> 17:18.044
Huh?

17:18.627 --> 17:20.880
- Yota!
- Kids!

17:20.963 --> 17:21.964
PIT PAT

17:22.840 --> 17:24.717
You gotta dry your hair first.

17:24.800 --> 17:26.093
Good grief.

17:26.177 --> 17:30.723
- Yota always just goes off to his room.
- Yeah!

17:30.806 --> 17:32.725
So we came to see you.

17:32.808 --> 17:35.936
- Yota, Yota...
- Go dry your hair. I'll wait.

17:36.020 --> 17:37.730
- You will?
- Yes.

17:37.813 --> 17:39.857
WHOOSH

17:39.940 --> 17:41.233
Goodness...

17:41.859 --> 17:45.654
Yota. There's ice cream in the freezer.
It's the good kind.

17:46.280 --> 17:48.491
But dinner first, okay?

17:48.574 --> 17:50.242
HMPH!

17:52.620 --> 17:56.916
<i>The kindness of others
is slowly seeping into my heart.</i>

17:59.710 --> 18:03.214
<i>How did I ever think I didn't belong?</i>

18:04.590 --> 18:05.758
<i>Soot...</i>

18:07.635 --> 18:11.889
<i>I see it now. I never realized it before.</i>

18:14.433 --> 18:16.519
<i>It's quiet tonight.</i>

18:18.395 --> 18:19.855
<i>It's been a while.</i>

18:22.608 --> 18:23.943
BREAD

18:24.026 --> 18:25.528
Did you sleep well last night?

18:25.611 --> 18:27.446
Yep. Like a log.

18:27.530 --> 18:28.531
I see.

18:30.199 --> 18:31.283
Huh?

18:32.034 --> 18:33.619
You got the drinks?

18:34.286 --> 18:35.287
Yeah.

18:35.371 --> 18:38.290
Hi, Amamiya. It's been a while.

18:39.708 --> 18:41.293
It has.

18:42.378 --> 18:43.379
What's this?

18:43.879 --> 18:45.840
It's my trio!

18:46.465 --> 18:48.300
- What a haul.
- What a haul.

18:49.468 --> 18:51.887
You're having bread
from the school store for lunch too?

18:51.971 --> 18:55.975
Get a load of this.
I left my lunch by the door at home today.

18:56.058 --> 18:57.184
Oh, dear.

18:57.268 --> 18:59.061
What? They still had sweet red bean buns?

18:59.145 --> 19:00.813
Yeah. Do you want it?

19:00.896 --> 19:02.898
No, no. I'll pay you. How much?

19:02.982 --> 19:03.983
WATCHING

19:04.066 --> 19:06.819
MIFFED

19:09.196 --> 19:10.823
HMM...

19:11.532 --> 19:13.200
It's fine. You can have it.

19:13.284 --> 19:15.161
No, let me pay.

19:15.244 --> 19:16.287
Then let's say, ten yen?

19:16.370 --> 19:18.455
No way was it ten yen.
Then let's at least trade.

19:19.415 --> 19:20.416
TUG

19:21.250 --> 19:22.585
Amamiya.

19:23.711 --> 19:25.588
What did you do over the winter break?

19:26.547 --> 19:28.007
<i>She initiated conversation.</i>

19:29.300 --> 19:32.803
I guess I mostly did club activities.

19:33.596 --> 19:36.348
I hung out with some classmates a bit,

19:36.849 --> 19:38.601
and took my dog for walks.

19:38.684 --> 19:39.894
Dog.

19:39.977 --> 19:41.103
FUZZY - DOG

19:42.229 --> 19:43.355
What else?

19:44.231 --> 19:49.320
<i>I always seem to put my foot in my mouth
whenever I talk to her.</i>

19:50.321 --> 19:52.740
<i>I never know what to do.</i>

19:53.782 --> 19:57.745
Hey. You got a name?

19:57.828 --> 19:58.829
Huh? Me?

19:58.913 --> 20:00.664
No. For the dog.

20:03.125 --> 20:05.085
Your first name is Minato, right?

20:08.380 --> 20:10.758
- It's Ponta.
- Huh?

20:10.841 --> 20:14.178
The dog! My name's not Ponta.

20:14.261 --> 20:15.804
<i>What am I even saying?</i>

20:15.888 --> 20:17.514
FLUSTER FLUSTER
PONTA AMAMIYA - PONTA

20:21.393 --> 20:23.979
Amamiya's first name... is "Ponta."

20:24.063 --> 20:27.149
Hey, could you not lose it over that?

20:28.400 --> 20:29.485
Sorry.

20:29.568 --> 20:30.653
SWEET RED BEAN BUN

20:30.736 --> 20:33.614
You really like your sweet red beans.
Don't you, Miki?

20:34.114 --> 20:36.492
Can't go wrong with sweet red beans!

20:36.575 --> 20:37.743
Right, Koyu--

20:37.826 --> 20:40.246
- Is Ponta doing well?
- Yeah.

20:40.329 --> 20:42.081
- I'm always taking photos.
- <i>Am I...</i>

20:42.164 --> 20:43.874
- Yeah?
- <i>Am I being a third wheel?</i>

20:43.958 --> 20:45.125
SHOCK

20:45.209 --> 20:46.710
<i>Koyun!</i>

20:48.087 --> 20:49.088
WHOMP - TAKE THAT - AH

20:49.171 --> 20:50.756
What was that for?

20:50.839 --> 20:51.840
SIGH

20:51.924 --> 20:54.176
I just got a surge of energy.

20:54.260 --> 20:56.679
That's your reason? You're dangerous.

20:58.764 --> 21:00.432
- Hey.
- I'm sorry.

21:00.516 --> 21:02.768
- You don't gotta force it.
- It's fine.

21:03.269 --> 21:04.353
SMILE GUARD

21:04.436 --> 21:05.938
Sorry. I couldn't help it.

21:06.522 --> 21:08.899
Now, look here! Don't make that face.

21:08.983 --> 21:09.984
SMILE GUARD ALPHA

21:10.067 --> 21:11.193
I'm sorry. I'm sorry!

21:11.277 --> 21:12.861
<i>What's this?</i>

21:13.654 --> 21:15.030
<i>Koyun and Yota...</i>

21:16.615 --> 21:19.451
- <i>They're getting on so well.</i>
- <i>They're getting on so well.</i>

21:19.535 --> 21:21.161
TODAY'S RECOMMENDATION
SAVORY BREAD FAIR

21:21.245 --> 21:22.454
I'll be going now.

21:22.538 --> 21:23.998
You're eating in again?

21:25.207 --> 21:27.376
- Yeah.
- <i>Eat in where?</i>

21:27.459 --> 21:28.627
NORIKO FROM THE NURSE'S OFFICE

21:28.711 --> 21:30.838
The nurse's office is not a café!

21:31.880 --> 21:33.215
I'll see you later.

21:33.841 --> 21:34.842
See you later.

21:39.305 --> 21:44.184
<i>Two people I like very much
seem to be hitting it off.</i>

21:44.268 --> 21:45.811
<i>That's all this is, so...</i>

21:47.021 --> 21:50.733
<i>So why does it get me so excited?</i>

21:52.067 --> 21:54.862
So, hey.
I know this is still a long ways off.

21:54.945 --> 21:58.324
But shall we have another four-way
study session for the end-of-year exams?

22:02.828 --> 22:04.997
- Sure.
- Hooray!

22:05.581 --> 22:07.916
<i>I'm gonna set those two up!</i>

22:08.000 --> 22:09.001
SO EXCITED

22:11.086 --> 22:13.839
- Hey, isn't that Miki?
- Okay! Time to study hard.

22:13.922 --> 22:18.260
And isn't that Hino and Amamiya with her?

22:19.845 --> 22:24.099
Is that how Miki usually behaves?

23:50.352 --> 23:55.357
Subtitle translation by: Rychelle Brittain
